QA3 C5, made runnable for QA4 m4. The value that reflection built is asserted
to its type in another function than the one that took it out of reflection.
The registry of reflect.Types is filled from a value of S, so S is exposed
there already; the assertion in another function is a second reason for the
same Unresolved entry (see reflect_type_kept_by_sync and the report of fix
round 5 for why a runnable program cannot have the second reason alone).
-- args --
a.go:@q
-- stdout --
$WORK/a.go:11:12-13: Error Set of example.com/x.F: 1 entries, 1 unresolved
$WORK/a.go:11:35-40: unresolved(memory): field Err of example.com/x.S may be written by reflection, unsafe code or a function that is not seen
	path (origin → target):
		$WORK/a.go:11:35-40: in example.com/x.F
-- go.mod --
module example.com/x

go 1.24
-- a.go --
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"reflect"
)

type S struct{ Err error }

func /*@q*/F(s *S) error { return s.Err }

func conv(a any) *S { return a.(*S) }

var registry = map[string]reflect.Type{}

func build(name string) any {
	v := reflect.New(registry[name])
	v.Elem().Field(0).Set(reflect.ValueOf(io.EOF))
	return v.Interface()
}

func main() {
	registry["s"] = reflect.TypeOf(S{})
	fmt.Println(F(conv(build("s"))))
}
